<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="MST Blockchain information, ecosystem, technology, MSTC and registration portal.">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#07111f">
  <title>MST Blockchain | MSTC Web3 Hub</title>
  <style>
    :root{
      --bg:#07111f; --bg2:#0b1728; --card:#0f2035; --line:#203752;
      --text:#f4f8ff; --muted:#a9b8ca; --accent:#43e0b3; --accent2:#6da7ff;
      --max:1150px;
    }
    *{box-sizing:border-box;scroll-behavior:smooth}
    body{margin:0;font-family:Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif;
      background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--bg),#091827 55%,#07111f);color:var(--text);line-height:1.65}
    a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
    .wrap{max-width:var(--max);margin:auto;padding:0 20px}
    nav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:20;background:rgba(7,17,31,.88);backdrop-filter:blur(14px);
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08)}
    .navin{height:70px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px}
    .logo{font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.08em;font-size:20px}
    .logo span{color:var(--accent)}
    .links{display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:center}
    .links a{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}
    .links a:hover{color:#fff}
    .btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:13px 18px;border-radius:12px;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),#35b8ff);color:#041019;font-weight:800;border:0;cursor:pointer}
    .btn.secondary{background:transparent;color:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line)}
    .hero{padding:95px 0 70px;position:relative;overflow:hidden}
    .hero:before{content:"";position:absolute;width:520px;height:520px;border-radius:50%;
      background:radial-gradient(circle,rgba(67,224,179,.18),transparent 68%);right:-180px;top:-180px}
    .badge{display:inline-block;padding:7px 12px;border:1px solid rgba(67,224,179,.3);
      color:var(--accent);border-radius:999px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;background:rgba(67,224,179,.06)}
    h1{font-size:clamp(42px,7vw,78px);line-height:1.02;margin:20px 0 18px;max-width:850px}
    h1 span{background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--accent),var(--accent2));-webkit-background-clip:text;color:transparent}
    .lead{font-size:19px;color:var(--muted);max-width:760px}
    .actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:28px}
    section{padding:72px 0}
    .eyebrow{color:var(--accent);font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;font-size:12px}
    h2{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,48px);margin:8px 0 14px;line-height:1.1}
    .sectionlead{color:var(--muted);max-width:760px}
    .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px;margin-top:28px}
    .card{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(15,32,53,.96),rgba(10,24,40,.96));
      border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;padding:24px}
    .card h3{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:20px}
    .card p{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}
    .stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px;margin-top:35px}
    .stat{padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.025)}
    .stat strong{display:block;font-size:28px;color:var(--accent)}
    .stat span{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}
    .two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:22px;align-items:stretch}
    .list{display:grid;gap:10px;margin-top:18px}
    .item{padding:13px 15px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;color:var(--muted)}
    .item b{color:#fff}
    .register{border:1px solid rgba(67,224,179,.28);background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 85% 15%,rgba(67,224,179,.12),transparent 35%),var(--card);
      border-radius:24px;padding:38px}
    .register p{color:var(--muted)}
    footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:35px 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}
    .notice{font-size:12px;color:#8293a8;margin-top:18px}
    .mobile{display:none}
    @media(max-width:800px){
      .links{display:none}.mobile{display:block}
      .grid,.stats,.two{grid-template-columns:1fr}
      .hero{padding-top:70px}
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <div class="wrap navin">
    <a class="logo" href="#home">MST<span>BLOCKCHAIN</span></a>
    <div class="links">
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="#technology">Technology</a>
      <a href="#ecosystem">Ecosystem</a>
      <a href="#usecases">Use Cases</a><a href="#network">Network</a><a href="#tokenomics">MSTC</a>
      <a href="#register">Register</a>
    </div>
    <a class="btn mobile" href="https://mstblockchain.com/portal/register/VeY52672" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Register</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<main id="home">
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="badge">PUBLIC • EVM-COMPATIBLE • LAYER 1</span>
      <h1>Explore the <span>MST Blockchain</span> ecosystem.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A modern information hub for MST Blockchain, MSTC, its technology, ecosystem,
        developer tools and registration portal.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="https://mstblockchain.com/portal/register/VeY52672" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Create / Register on MST
        </a>
        <a class="btn secondary" href="https://mstscan.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Open MST Explorer
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><strong>3.0s</strong><span>Average block time</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>4000+</strong><span>TPS claimed in MST materials</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>0.001</strong><span>MSTC average fee shown on MST site</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>EVM</strong><span>Ethereum-compatible development</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section id="about">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">01 / About</div>
      <h2>What is MST Blockchain?</h2>
      <p class="sectionlead">
        MST Blockchain describes itself as a public, EVM-compatible Layer-1 blockchain
        developed by Masterstroke Technosoft. Its materials describe low-cost transactions,
        fast block processing and support for decentralized applications.
      </p>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Layer 1</h3><p>MST operates as an independent blockchain network rather than an application-layer token on another chain.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>MSTC</h3><p>MSTC is the native coin used for network utility such as transaction fees and protocol functions.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>EVM Compatible</h3><p>Developers can use familiar Ethereum tooling such as Solidity, MetaMask, Remix and Hardhat.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="technology">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">02 / Technology</div>
      <h2>Core technology</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>PoSA</h3><p>MST documentation describes a Proof of Staked Authority consensus design for validator-based network operation.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Fast finality</h3><p>MST materials state an average block time of approximately 3 seconds and rapid transaction finality.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Smart Contracts</h3><p>Solidity-based smart contracts and EVM-compatible decentralized applications can be deployed using common Web3 tools.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>DAO Governance</h3><p>MST's whitepaper describes staking, delegation and on-chain governance mechanisms.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Developer Friendly</h3><p>Ethereum-compatible tools reduce the learning curve for developers already familiar with EVM networks.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Data & Verification</h3><p>The ecosystem highlights blockchain-based certificates, document verification and auditable records.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="ecosystem">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">03 / Ecosystem</div>
      <h2>Products & protocols</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>SARAL Protocol</h3><p>A simplified SDK/web protocol intended to make on-chain onboarding easier.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>WASMify</h3><p>A protocol described by MST for connecting Web2 processing with Web3 verification.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>BridgeKey</h3><p>A multi-chain wallet product presented as part of the MST ecosystem.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>MST Buddy</h3><p>An AI-powered assistant for learning about and interacting with the MST ecosystem.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>ProofEasy</h3><p>A blockchain-powered document verification product associated with the MST ecosystem.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>ChainPay</h3><p>A crypto payment gateway presented on the MST Blockchain ecosystem site.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="usecases">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">04 / Use Cases</div>
      <h2>What can be built on MST?</h2>
      <div class="two">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="list">
            <div class="item"><b>RWA:</b> tokenized real estate and other real-world assets</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Carbon:</b> carbon-credit tracking</div>
            <div class="item"><b>NFT:</b> NFT ticketing and digital ownership</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Identity:</b> digital identity and KYC systems</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Supply Chain:</b> transparent product tracking</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Certificates:</b> verifiable on-chain credentials</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Gaming:</b> blockchain-based asset ownership</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Governance:</b> decentralized voting and DAO applications</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>For developers</h3>
          <p>
            Build Solidity smart contracts, connect a wallet, deploy an EVM dApp and
            use blockchain transactions for verification and application logic.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn secondary" href="https://github.com/mst-chain" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MST GitHub</a>
            <a class="btn secondary" href="https://github.com/mst-chain/whitepaper" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Whitepaper</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section id="network">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">05 / Network</div>
      <h2>MST Network Details</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Consensus</h3><p>Official MST whitepaper describes Parlia, a Proof of Staked Authority (PoSA) consensus design with stake-based validator selection.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Finality</h3><p>MST's whitepaper describes fast finality, with approximately 3-second blocks and finality after two block confirmations.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Validator Set</h3><p>Validators are selected according to total stake, including self-stake and delegated stake; the whitepaper also describes standby validators and slashing.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Governance</h3><p>Staking credits, delegation, proposals, voting and timelocked execution are described in MST's on-chain governance framework.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Native Asset</h3><p>MSTC is described as the native coin used for transaction fees, validator incentives, governance and network utility.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Developer Stack</h3><p>EVM compatibility supports familiar Ethereum tooling such as MetaMask, Remix, Hardhat and Truffle.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="tokenomics">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">06 / Tokenomics</div>
      <h2>MSTC Tokenomics</h2>
      <div class="two">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>According to the MST Whitepaper</h3>
          <div class="list">
            <div class="item"><b>Genesis supply:</b> 50 billion MSTC</div>
            <div class="item"><b>2024 burn:</b> whitepaper states a major burn on December 31, 2024</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Stated post-burn circulation:</b> 8,401,387,498 MSTC</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Initial block reward:</b> 200 MSTC per block</div>
            <div class="item"><b>Halving:</b> described as occurring every two years</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Important</h3>
          <p>
            Token supply, circulating supply, rewards and market data can change.
            This page presents statements from MST's published materials and is not
            investment advice or a guarantee of future token value or returns.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn secondary" href="https://github.com/mst-chain/whitepaper" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read Whitepaper</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="malayalam">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">07 / Malayalam</div>
      <h2>MST Blockchain — മലയാളത്തിൽ</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          MST Blockchain ഒരു Layer-1 blockchain network ആണ്. MSTയുടെ ഔദ്യോഗിക whitepaper
          പ്രകാരം ഇത് EVM-compatible ആണ്, അതിനാൽ Solidity smart contract, MetaMask, Remix,
          Hardhat തുടങ്ങിയ tools ഉപയോഗിച്ച് applications നിർമ്മിക്കാം. MSTC ആണ് network-ന്റെ
          native coin. Consensus ആയി Parlia / Proof of Staked Authority (PoSA) സംവിധാനം
          whitepaper വിവരിക്കുന്നു.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top:15px">
          Staking, delegation, validator participation, DAO-style governance, NFT, RWA,
          supply-chain, document verification, carbon-credit തുടങ്ങിയ use cases-ുകൾ
          MST ecosystem-ൽ നിർമ്മിക്കാവുന്നതാണ്. ഉപയോഗിക്കുന്ന application-നും token activity-ക്കും
          ബാധകമായ local laws പ്രത്യേകം പരിശോധിക്കണം.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="register">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="register">
        <div class="eyebrow">08 / Registration</div>
        <h2>Join MST Blockchain</h2>
        <p>
          Use the registration/referral link supplied for this website. The button opens
          the MST portal directly in a new tab.
        </p>
        <a class="btn" href="https://mstblockchain.com/portal/register/VeY52672" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          REGISTER NOW
        </a>
        <p class="notice">
          Note: This website is an independent information/landing page. It is not an
          official MST Blockchain website unless separately authorized by MST. Registration,
          token use, staking, investment and other activities may be subject to applicable
          laws and the terms of the relevant service.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="sources">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">09 / Official Sources</div>
      <h2>Verify the information</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>MST Blockchain</h3><p>Official MST website and portal.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn secondary" href="https://mstblockchain.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Official Site</a></div></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>MST GitHub</h3><p>Public repositories published by the MST Chain GitHub organization.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn secondary" href="https://github.com/mst-chain" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open GitHub</a></div></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>MST Whitepaper</h3><p>Technical architecture, consensus, validators, tokenomics and governance.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn secondary" href="https://github.com/mst-chain/whitepaper/blob/main/WHITEPAPER.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Whitepaper</a></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<footer>
  <div class="wrap">
    <strong>AJJRA TECHNO HUB • MST Blockchain Information Hub</strong><br>
    Independent information website built by AJJRA TECHNO HUB and designed for GitHub Pages. MST trademarks, services and claims belong
    to their respective owners.
  </div>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
